## 5. Kafka KRaft configuration

Kafka 3.9.2 supports KRaft operation without ZooKeeper.

The clean functional test uses:

| Setting | Value |
|---|---|
| Node ID | 1 |
| Broker listener | 127.0.0.1:19092 |
| Controller listener | 127.0.0.1:19093 |
| Metadata mode | KRaft |
| Replication factor | 1 |
| Partitions | 1 |

Create the isolated test configuration:

```bash
TEST_DATA="$WORK/kafka-clean-test-data"

mkdir -p "$TEST_DATA/data"

cat > "$TEST_DATA/server.properties" <<EOF
process.roles=broker,controller
node.id=1

controller.quorum.voters=1@127.0.0.1:19093

listeners=PLAINTEXT://127.0.0.1:19092,CONTROLLER://127.0.0.1:19093

advertised.listeners=PLAINTEXT://127.0.0.1:19092

listener.security.protocol.map=PLAINTEXT:PLAINTEXT,CONTROLLER:PLAINTEXT

inter.broker.listener.name=PLAINTEXT
controller.listener.names=CONTROLLER

log.dirs=$TEST_DATA/data

num.partitions=1

offsets.topic.replication.factor=1
transaction.state.log.replication.factor=1
transaction.state.log.min.isr=1

group.initial.rebalance.delay.ms=0
EOF
```

### 5.1 Format storage

Storage formatting is a one-time operation for a new empty data directory.

```bash
CLUSTER_ID=$("$KAFKA/bin/kafka-storage.sh" random-uuid)

echo "$CLUSTER_ID" > "$TEST_DATA/cluster-id.txt"

"$KAFKA/bin/kafka-storage.sh" format \
    --cluster-id "$CLUSTER_ID" \
    --config "$TEST_DATA/server.properties"
```

**Never format an existing Kafka data directory.**

Do not reuse the earlier failed test metadata directory.

### 5.2 Start Kafka

```bash
export KAFKA_HEAP_OPTS="-Xms512M -Xmx512M"

nohup "$KAFKA/bin/kafka-server-start.sh" \
    "$TEST_DATA/server.properties" \
    > "$TEST_DATA/kafka-server.log" 2>&1 \
    < /dev/null &
```

Check listeners:

```bash
ss -lntp | grep -E ':19092|:19093'
```

Check logs:

```bash
tail -60 "$TEST_DATA/kafka-server.log"
```

### 5.3 Verify the broker

```bash
"$KAFKA/bin/kafka-broker-api-versions.sh" \
    --bootstrap-server 127.0.0.1:19092
```

Verify KRaft quorum:

```bash
"$KAFKA/bin/kafka-metadata-quorum.sh" \
    --bootstrap-server 127.0.0.1:19092 \
    describe --status
```

### 5.4 Create a test topic

```bash
TOPIC="offline-source-build-test"

"$KAFKA/bin/kafka-topics.sh" \
    --bootstrap-server 127.0.0.1:19092 \
    --create --if-not-exists \
    --topic "$TOPIC" \
    --partitions 1 \
    --replication-factor 1
```

Describe:

```bash
"$KAFKA/bin/kafka-topics.sh" \
    --bootstrap-server 127.0.0.1:19092 \
    --describe --topic "$TOPIC"
```

### 5.5 Produce and consume a message

Produce:

```bash
MESSAGE="KAFKA_SOURCE_BUILD_OFFLINE_PASS"

printf '%s\n' "$MESSAGE" | \
    "$KAFKA/bin/kafka-console-producer.sh" \
    --bootstrap-server 127.0.0.1:19092 \
    --topic "$TOPIC"
```

Consume:

```bash
"$KAFKA/bin/kafka-console-consumer.sh" \
    --bootstrap-server 127.0.0.1:19092 \
    --topic "$TOPIC" \
    --from-beginning \
    --max-messages 1 \
    --timeout-ms 20000
```

The consumer must receive the exact produced message.

